  "explanation": "Attention Rollout (Abnar & Zuidema, 2020) quantifies cumulative information flow through multi-layer Transformers. Because representations pass through both multi-head attention and residual bypass highways (x = x + f(x)), isolated single-layer attention matrices only reflect local routing. By recursively accumulating adjusted attention matrices across all 6 layers, rollout reveals how much information from each input token reached the final prediction position. In GPT-2 architectures, position 0 ('The') frequently acts as an attention sink, absorbing 92.0% of cumulative flow, while later tokens contribute fine-grained syntactic and semantic context.",
